# Hover, overlays, and clipping

Floating UI and hover-lift effects must never be clipped by ancestor overflow.

## Floating overlays — always portal

Tooltips, hover cards, popovers, menus, and hand-rolled suggestion menus must render via a Portal (Radix `*.Portal` or `createPortal(..., document.body)`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — clipped by overflow-y-auto ancestors
<TooltipPrimitive.Content>...</TooltipPrimitive.Content>

// ✅ GOOD
<TooltipPrimitive.Portal>
  <TooltipPrimitive.Content collisionPadding={8} className="z-[70]">...</TooltipPrimitive.Content>
</TooltipPrimitive.Portal>
```

Use `z-[70]` for tip/hover-card content so it sits above `z-50` dialogs/sheets when both are open.

## Hover lift — reserve a gutter

`.card-lift` paints outside its box (`translateY(-1px)` + outer ring). Any scroll/clip ancestor that holds lift cards must use `.lift-gutter` (or equivalent padding + negative margin):

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="overflow-y-auto pr-1 space-y-2">{/* card-lift rows */}</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="overflow-y-auto lift-gutter space-y-2">{/* card-lift rows */}</div>
```

Do not put `.lift-gutter` on the same element as a visible border unless you wrap an inner scroller — negative margin fights the border box.

## Persistent state — use outline, not ring/box-shadow

`.card-lift:hover` sets `box-shadow`. That overrides Tailwind `ring-*` and other `box-shadow` state styles. Use `outline` with a negative offset for selection / needs-assignee / unclaimed edges:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hover wipe
selected && "ring-2 ring-info ring-offset-1"

// ✅ GOOD
selected && "outline outline-2 outline-info -outline-offset-2"
```

## Checklist before shipping card UI

1. Overlay content is portaled.
2. Nearest `overflow-*` ancestor of `.card-lift` has `.lift-gutter` (or vertical equivalent).
3. Selection / urgency indicators use `outline`, not competing `box-shadow`/`ring`.
